## Finding: TOCTOU in the outbox duplicate check (new)
- In postAs (internal/comms/commands.go at the tip): `findOutboxByHash(from, hash)` runs at ~line 183, `b.lockBus()` is taken only afterwards (~line 195), and the record is NOT re-checked under the lock.
- Consequence: two concurrent identical remote sends (same summary+target+domain+msgType+replyTo) both find no record; the first writes the pending record (deterministic ID → same path), publishes, sets ExternalID; the second then overwrites the same record with ExternalID="" and publishes AGAIN. Each publish uses a fresh random external ID (internal/wormhole/messages.go:99), so the wormhole-side idempotency (same bytes+same ID → re-publish; different → fail-closed) does NOT catch it → true duplicate on the wire.
- Master (e060e2e) has the same check with no lock at all, so the branch is an improvement but does not close this hole.
- Suggested fix: move the findOutboxByHash check inside the lock (or repeat it after lockBus()). Sequential retry is already handled correctly (pending record found by hash in unseen/+seen/+flat); the concurrent case is untested.

